From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Trace the PS4 Vulkan instance creation boundary

The hang after DXVK lists instance extensions occurs before any physical-device
format or device-extension log. Mark the conversion and host vkCreateInstance
boundaries so a console log distinguishes Wine-side conversion from a RADV
call that does not return.

The messages use the vulkan debug channel; enable warn+vulkan for the target
profile during this diagnostic.

--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -610,8 +610,13 @@
     list_init( &instance->utils_messengers );
     list_init( &instance->report_callbacks );
 
+    WARN( "PS4 Vulkan instance phase=convert-begin extensions=%u layers=%u\n",
+          create_info->enabledExtensionCount, create_info->enabledLayerCount );
     if ((res = convert_instance_create_info( &pool, create_info, instance ))) goto failed;
+    WARN( "PS4 Vulkan instance phase=convert-end res=%d\n", res );
+    WARN( "PS4 Vulkan instance phase=host-create-begin\n" );
     if ((res = p_vkCreateInstance( create_info, NULL /* allocator */, &host_instance ))) goto failed;
+    WARN( "PS4 Vulkan instance phase=host-create-end res=%d host=%p\n", res, host_instance );
 
     vulkan_object_init_ptr( &instance->obj.obj, (UINT_PTR)host_instance, &client_instance->obj );
     instance->obj.p_insert_object = vulkan_instance_insert_object;
